Z||000000||gtjeff||12-30-2001||03:31 PM||||Anyone know the slalom time for the 88 gt-I have seen slalom times for earlier models(like around 63.5 mph), but not the 88 gt. Just wondering how much of a difference the revised suspension makes in the mph time. thanks jeff||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||12-30-2001||04:20 PM||||Motor Trend March 1988 has a skidpad of 0.84, 0-60 in 8.72 and 1/4mi of 16.44@81.9. Sorry, no slalom. <P>A new 88 GT was $16,087 (as tested) though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://centralillinoisimports.org/uploads/files/SigRear4.gif">  <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||12-30-2001||05:43 PM||||.84 is all the 88gt got??? Thats pretty lame.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jncomutt||12-30-2001||06:51 PM||||Well that may be lame but the December 1983 issue of Car and Driver rated the 2M4 at .79<P>The November 1984 issue of Motor Trend rated the 85GT at .82<P>So, .84 actually was an improvement over previous years..||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||12-31-2001||05:02 PM||||Remenber also that the tires GM put on our cars flagrantly sucked.<P>With just some good 17"s, a fresh suspension 88 will turn nearly one gee all day long.  Lower it an inch to make that over one gee.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
